        ":question/problem": "If \n$W=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$, then $\\text{rank}(W)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the rank of $H,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(W)=3.$"
