        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-35271",
        ":question/problem": "If \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$, then $\\text{rank}(B)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the rank of $B,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(B)=2.$"
