        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-35273",
        ":question/problem": "If \n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, find $\\text{rank}(F).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the rank of $F,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 14 & 13 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(F)=3.$"
